{
 "about": "Per-angle colour correction + unified black level, baked into the plates by render.py prep --vf. Chain: yuv(bt709 tv) -> gbrp16le; lutrgb per channel y = shoulder(gain * toe(x)), toe = normalised softplus black offset d (k = 4/d, 1 -> 1), quadratic highlight shoulder only on channels with gain > 1 (input 1 -> exactly 1, no clip); optional Rec.709 luma-preserving saturation (colorchannelmixer); optional master low-mid bump (L1 floor); -> yuv444p16le bt709 tv; prep then converts to yuvj420p JPEG q3 exactly as before. Targets: void mean 2.6/255 neutral (= L4's own void); neutral axis (grey beard) and skin level/chroma of L4 (main angle). Measured on 10 frames per clip; global plate look (contrast 1.05 saturate .93 brightness 1.01 + soft-light rgba(52,78,96) .14 + vignette .2) simulated in headless Chromium with the engine canvas ops (work/grade/look.js).",
 "sample_frames": [
  60,
  360,
  660,
  960,
  1260,
  1560,
  1860,
  2160,
  2460,
  2760
 ],
